# Graphify exclusions. Git ignore is disabled during the build, so dependency,
# build, cache, log and temp trees are listed here instead. Required Markdown
# folders (.ai/, specs/, .specify/, plans/, docs/) stay IN the graph.

# Build output and caches
target/
.ci-work/
.ci-*/
node_modules/
dist/
.cargo/
graphify-out/
.codebase-memory/
.codebase-memory*/
*.profraw

# Runtime data written by a real run; not source
Output/
Logs/
User/
*.mbclaim
*.uplock
*.mbstate*
*.lock

# Transient staging/derived trees, not project knowledge
.ai/.cross-project-sync/
.ai/ARCHIVE/
# Private notes and signing metadata. Never graphed, never surfaced in a query
# answer, even when a future file here looks like ordinary documentation.
.ai/PRIVATE/

# Agent configuration and local instruction files
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.kiro/
.cursor/
.cline/
secrets.md
.ignoreme
explain-AI.md
.env
.env.*

# Test fixtures mirror the Rust surface one-for-one; they add ~700
# nodes of near-duplicate names and push the graph past the 5000-node
# aggregation threshold for the HTML view.
tests/
